<item><title>MLSTP fails to form government after election win</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/mlstp-fails-to-form-government-after-election-win-d8cc8c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/mlstp-fails-to-form-government-after-election-win-d8cc8c/</guid><category>Sao Tome and Principe</category><description>The ADI party, which finished second, secured a 29-seat majority with the MCI-PS/PUN coalition, and its leader Américo d&apos;Oliveira dos Ramos was named Prime Minister on November 12.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:03:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/st.jpg" length="38731" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/st.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>President names ADI leader Américo Ramos prime minister</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/president-names-adi-leader-americo-ramos-prime-minister-d8a377/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/president-names-adi-leader-americo-ramos-prime-minister-d8a377/</guid><category>Sao Tome and Principe</category><description>Carlos Vila Nova chose Ramos after the MLSTP, which won the most seats, could not show it had enough parliamentary support to govern.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:37:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/president-names-adi-leader-americo-ramos-prime-minister-d8a377/share.jpg" length="41396" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/president-names-adi-leader-americo-ramos-prime-minister-d8a377/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Central bank asks public to take part in emigration and currency survey</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/central-bank-asks-public-to-take-part-in-emigration-and-28ae00/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/st/central-bank-asks-public-to-take-part-in-emigration-and-28ae00/</guid><category>Sao Tome and Principe</category><description>The Central Bank of Sao Tome and Principe is collecting views on emigration, the foreign exchange market and inflation expectations until November 22.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:22:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/st.jpg" length="38731" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/st.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
